{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-gb-spectral-sequence-intro","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:gb-spectral-sequence-intro","kind":"prose","title":"Six mass terms as spectral-sequence pages","text":"gb-spectral-sequence-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:gb-spectral-sequence-intro\"></a><p>The descending Gröbner–Shirshov ideal filtration <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^\\bullet(q)</code> on the Iwahori–Hecke algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code> induces a spectral sequence. For semisimple <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_n(R, q)</code> its limit page is concentrated in total degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code>, and its <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E_\\infty</code> page governs homological shell condensation and the motivic Galois coaction per cell.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/gb-spectral-sequence-intro.md","heading":"","page":"b/sec-gb-spectral-sequence-intro","qa":{"counts":{"pass":42,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":23,"unknown":0,"stale":65}}}
